@startuml
title Option B — normal critical delivery with a durable workflow
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor "Bank service" as Producer
participant "Notification API" as API
database "Admission PostgreSQL\n+ start/receipt outbox" as Index
participant "Relay + Kafka\nWorkflow starter" as Starter
participant "Temporal Service\n+ durable history DB" as Temporal
participant "Go Workflow /\nActivity workers" as Worker
participant "FCM / APNs" as Push
actor "Bank app" as App
participant "Receipt Gateway" as Receipt

Producer -> API: Submit(logical_key)
API -> Index: Atomic unique inbox + notification + start_outbox
Index --> API: Synchronous durable commit
API --> Producer: 202 Accepted (durable admission)
Starter -> Index: Read committed start_outbox
Starter -> Temporal: StartWorkflow(ID=logical_key, RejectDuplicate)
Temporal -> Temporal: Persist WorkflowExecutionStarted
Temporal --> Starter: Started / AlreadyStarted
note over Starter, Temporal: Retrying start after a crash cannot create a second logical workflow.\nAdmission unique-key retention also covers completed histories.
Temporal -> Worker: Workflow task
Worker -> Temporal: Schedule push activity + durable 8s timer
Temporal -> Worker: Activity task(attempt_id)
Worker -> Push: Send(notification_id, stable attempt_id, TTL=8s)
Push --> Worker: Provider accepted
Worker -> Temporal: Activity result (acceptance only)
Push -> App: Push
App -> App: Persistent dedup(notification_id)
App -> Receipt: Authenticated received ACK
Receipt -> Index: Atomic receipt inbox + receipt_outbox; COMMIT
Starter -> Temporal: Signal(receipt_id, notification_id, delivered evidence)
Temporal -> Temporal: Persist signal in workflow history
Temporal -> Worker: Workflow task with receipt
Worker -> Worker: Workflow dedup by receipt_id
Worker -> Temporal: DELIVERED; cancel future timers / activities
Starter -> Index: Project delivered business status asynchronously
note over Index, Temporal: History is the delivery-state authority.\nThe business index is a rebuildable read projection.
@enduml
